                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is absolutely not good by any means, and can be frustrating and confusing at times, but it was still an interesting experience worth trying out if you like low budget indie horror games like this. The negative things I have to say about this game is that the concept of the game isn't executed the best, I guess the \"owners\" of the house are some white goblin monster, a massive white baby, a nude white girl with a knife, and some random bald dude with a hammer who just fucking dies instantly. Some parts of the game can be very confusing, which is probably why they added an option to view your objective, but the objective is a bit vague and not clear on what to exactly do sometimes. This game used to have pretty normal pictures in the houses picture frames, but they where replaced with scary disturbing ones, with one of them being just plain gross, with the picture being a seemingly real picture of a naked overweight woman turned away from the camera, so I recommend playing the old version of this game that was posted on an itch account called \"Indie Horror Archive 666\", and why are we turning off the lights in the house if we know that one of the creatures don't like the light... The positives I do have to say about this game, it is an interesting concept, and the animation is not bad.",
